  "scientific_scope_status": "For finite Gaussian paths X_z(t)=mu+B(t)z with z standard N(0,I_n), an available h produces a uniformly interior trajectory with facet slack >=r||a_i||_1. For theta=eta/r<1, T(z)=(1-theta)z+theta h satisfies gamma(TA)>=exp(-beta)gamma(A) for every measurable A, beta=-n log(1-theta)+theta||h||^2/[2(2-theta)]. Completing the Gaussian density square proves the sharp measurable-set constant. A nondegenerate supplied constant mode gives h with ||h||^2=(x_star-mu)^T S0^-1(x_star-mu); strict interior data are acquired by charged rational LP/linear algebra, not a supplied rare witness.",
